{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_last_stage_theorem", "label": "FILL-OUTSIDE \u2014 the tower has no limit to take, it has a last stage", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-OUTSIDE-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With finitely many independent labels, \u03a3(1 \u2212 ratio) is a finite sum and L = fill(D_last) > 0 \u2014 so L = 0 is excluded from outside though it was admissible from inside. Closure could not see this because closure never gives reference: it cannot tell a measurement from a repetition of one."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_finite_labels_premise", "label": "The outside premise \u2014 a bound transition has finitely many independent labels", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-OUTSIDE-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prior-art physics (Condon & Shortley 1935; Cowan 1981): two finite-dimensional multiplets, one nucleus, one projection each \u2014 a finite complete set, so the ladder ends."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_hyperfine_rung_f", "label": "The hyperfine rung F = J \u2297 I and its projection m_F", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-OUTSIDE-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In one-parent envelope form both bounds are monotone functions of one parent, hence morphisms, hence closed (E = 0 on six exhaustive tests); the exact triangle with its parity congruence does not close, exactly as E3 and \u00a712.11.6 say. At I = 0 the rung is a RELABEL, so the hyperfine axis exists only for I \u2265 \u00bd."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_measurement_doctrine", "label": "An axis that lowers fill is a measurement, not a function of what is there", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-OUTSIDE-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Theorem 11.1 and \u00a732.1.4: \u211b never produces a coordinate, and a function of existing coordinates adjoined as a coordinate would lower fill while measuring nothing \u2014 the doctrine refuses it as an axis."}], "edges": [{"source": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_last_stage_theorem", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_limit_finding_fill_limit_undecidable", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-OUTSIDE-FINDING.md", "source_location": "header", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_last_stage_theorem", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_finite_labels_premise", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-OUTSIDE-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a71\u2013\u00a72", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_last_stage_theorem", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_hyperfine_rung_f", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-OUTSIDE-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_measurement_doctrine", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_outside_finding_last_stage_theorem", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-OUTSIDE-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1.0}, {"sour